/P 100 0 R
/E (LFIGP has long been a diverse, international community. With students representing numerous nationalities, the school thus offers an environment where different cultures, perspectives, and ideas come together. LFIGPMUN builds on this identity, bringing the principles of diplomacy, cooperation, debate, and international understanding into the conference room.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (Model United Nations is more than a simulation; it is an opportunity to step into the role of a diplomat and experience the complexity of international decision-making. Throughout the conference, delegates will be challenged to conduct thorough research, speak confidently, negotiate respectfully, collaborate with others, and defend the interests of the countries they represent.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (Since this is our inaugural conference, every delegate has the chance to help shape the legacy of LFIGPMUN. The resolutions drafted, debates held, partnerships formed, and ideas exchanged during this conference will establish the groundwork for a tradition we hope will carry on for many years to come.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (Whether this is your first MUN conference or you are an experienced delegate, remember that your voice matters. Do not be afraid to speak, question, negotiate, compromise, or propose something new.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
